<title>GREECE: GREEK MAY CORE INFLATION RISES TO 7.6PCT Y/Y-BOGR.</title>
<headline>GREEK MAY CORE INFLATION RISES TO 7.6PCT Y/Y-BOGR.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's core inflation which does not include volatile food and fuels prices rose to 7.6 percent year-on-year in May from 7.4 percent in April, central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Underlying or core inflation figures are based on the OECD definition.</p>
<p>Headline consumer price inflation dropped to 5.4 percent year-on-year in May from 5.9 percent in April.</p>
<p>			 Headline inflation	Core inflation</p>
<p>				 (%)			 (%)</p>
<p>    May	 97	   5.4			 7.6</p>
<p>    April     97	   5.9			 7.4</p>
<p>    March     97	   6.0			 7.4</p>
<p>    February  97	   6.5			 7.2</p>
<p>    January   97	   6.8			 7.1</p>
<p>    December  96	   7.3			 7.8</p>
<p>    November  96	   7.5			 7.9</p>
<p>    October   96	   8.0			 8.1</p>
<p>    September 96	   7.9			 7.8</p>
<p>    August    96	   8.0			 8.0</p>
<p>    July	96	   8.1			 8.2</p>
<p>    June	96	   8.4			 8.4</p>
<p>    May	 96	   8.7			 8.7</p>
